It builds on publicly shared Kaggle notebooks for the Kaggriculture competition,
all of which were published under the Apache License 2.0. Their complete license
texts and attribution notices are retained verbatim inside the agent sources that
embed them (for example agent/c1200_final.py and the agent/public_*.py files).
Upstream works include, among others:

- Kaito Fukami, "25/27 Strict-Future | v27 Midgame Meta Reset" (route backbone credited to Ezzzzzekki)
- Ahmed Berat Ozer, "More Yield, Smarter Labor" (V37) and "Kaggriculture V54 Productive Wheat and Patient"
- Guru Prasaath S, "Kaggriculture Master Engine V2"
- Seyit Kaan Gunes, "Kaggriculture 2820 score" (shop-aware herd substitution layer)
- Dmitrii Gluzdov, "More Wheat, Smarter Sales" and "Herd-Safe Sale Window"
- Harvey Zhang, "V15 Market Stack"
- xox787, "Terminal Recovery v4"
- Thomas Tschinkel, router v5 (used as a reference opponent)
- Further public notebooks embedded only as opponent-policy hypotheses for state tracking;
  each is attributed inside the embedding source.

Kaggle competition data were used only under the competition rules. Raw episode
replays, competition payloads and local league databases are not part of this
repository.
